// @generated by website/scripts/sync-docs.mjs from docs/WRITING_MAXON_CODE.md (its preamble and its "## Scripts and scriptlib" section); edit that document and run the script, never this file
let McpAgentInstructions ="ALWAYS read this document, `WRITING_MAXON_CODE.md`, before writing or modifying Maxon code. An install\nholds it in `docs/`, beside `stdlib/`, with the documents it links.\nFor the full specification see [LANGUAGE_REFERENCE.md](LANGUAGE_REFERENCE.md) and [BNF_SYNTAX.md](BNF_SYNTAX.md);\nfor the standard library's API see [STDLIB_REFERENCE.md](STDLIB_REFERENCE.md).\n\nWhen a build or test run reports breaking changes since the project was last built, call the MCP\n`breaking_changes` tool and apply each change's fix. See\n[Breaking changes since the last build](CLI_REFERENCE.md#breaking-changes-since-the-last-build).\n\n`maxon build` leaves the [lint rules](CLI_REFERENCE.md#maxon-lint) to `maxon lint`: a discarded result\n(**E3064**, **E3065**), an unused `export` (**E3092**) and an unused unexported declaration (**E3219**).\nBefore handing code back, run `maxon lint` on the program, and `maxon lint --tests` on a project's tests,\nor call the MCP `check` tool, which enforces them too. `maxon lint --fix` rewrites the files with the repair\nof every finding that has exactly one, and reports the rest.\n\n## Scripts and scriptlib\n\nPut a helper in a **scriptlib** package only when two or more single-file scripts need it. Keep out of\nscriptlib:\n\n- Code only one script uses: keep it in that script.\n- Code for a directory project: put it in the project's own files.\n- Anything meant to ship to everyone: that belongs in the standard library (`stdlib/`).\n\nLay out, write and call a package as [The scriptlib directory](CLI_REFERENCE.md#the-scriptlib-directory)\nsays, and run [`maxon check-scriptlib`](CLI_REFERENCE.md#maxon-check-scriptlib) after editing one."
